  Rewrite by m0us3r - https://github.com/mym0us3r/Unified-Sysmon-Configs
  Date: 03/27/2026 Friday :)

  Sysmon EventChannel Infrastructure + Process Anomaly rules: 61600 - 61643
  Rewritten for Sysmon Native (Windows 11 24H2+)
  Provider: Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon
  EID 1: Process Creation - Infrastructure routing and process anomaly detection
  MITRE ATT&CK v15 aligned

  ESCAPING REFERENCE (critical):
    Wazuh decoder doubles backslashes in Windows paths.
    Stored internally: C:\\Windows\\System32\\cmd.exe (double backslash)
    PCRE2 to match \\: use \\\\
    Rule: path separators -> \\\\ | regex meta (\s \d \b \.) -> \\

  MIGRATION NOTES:
    Infrastructure rules (61600-61651): preserved as-is. Required for all EID routing.
    Process anomaly rules (61618-61641): ANCHOR FIX applied.
    if_sid>92000 replaced by if_group>sysmon_event1 + providerName field check.
    Reason: if_group references a runtime group tag, not a compile-time rule ID.
    Group sysmon_event1 is defined by rule 61603 (in this same file, above) at
    event processing time - zero load-order dependency.
    if_sid>92000 was silently failing because 0595 loads before 0800 alphabetically,
    so 92000 did not exist at load time.
    Frequency rules (61642-61643): preserved as-is.
-->

<var name="MS_FREQ">8</var>

